<p>Ukraine launched one of its largest drone barrages against Russia overnight into Sunday, killing at least four people, including three in the Moscow region and one in the Belgorod region, Russian authorities said. Russia’s defense ministry said air defenses intercepted or shot down 556 drones across 14 Russian regions, Crimea and the Black and Azov seas; Dawn, citing Russian officials, reported another 30 drones intercepted after dawn. Moscow faced its biggest drone attack in more than a year, with Russian state agency TASS citing Mayor Sergei Sobyanin as saying 81 drones headed for the capital had been destroyed since midnight. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the strikes were “entirely justified” after Russia’s recent drone and missile bombardment of Kyiv killed at least 24 people. Russian officials said residential buildings and infrastructure were damaged in the Moscow region, while Moscow’s Sheremetyevo airport said drone debris fell on its grounds without causing damage. Russia’s Foreign Ministry accused Kyiv of targeting civilians; both sides deny deliberately targeting civilians in the war.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/fkdAG1oMQI-4sc8k9DvgJModqW4gQgj01F5ak9OZ0N63YEHZ1kShLlpm8paVYQDJerNgYAMx_50l5hWDhlCXqvKoC-LmLQBg-KUQWkJDkQ' alt='An apartment building damaged in a Ukrainian drone attack in Krasnogorsk, in the Moscow region, Russia, on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Local casualties: Moscow regional Governor Andrei Vorobyov said a woman died when a home was hit in Khimki, north of the capital, and two men were killed in Pogorelki in the Mytishchi district. He said rescuers were searching the Khimki debris for another person.</li><li>Refinery area: Sobyanin said 12 people were injured, most near the entrance to Moscow’s oil refinery, but said the refinery’s “technology” was not damaged.</li><li>Drone totals: The New Arab reported that Russia’s defense ministry said more than 1,000 Ukrainian drones had been downed over the country in the preceding 24 hours.</li></ul><blockquote>Our responses to Russia’s prolongation of the war and its attacks on our cities and communities are entirely justified. This time, Ukrainian long-range sanctions reached the Moscow region, and we are clearly telling the Russians: their state must end its war. - Volodymyr Zelensky</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukraine’s Defense Ministry: The ministry said Moscow and the surrounding region faced the largest drone attack since Russia’s full-scale invasion and that several strategic facilities were struck for the first time. (<a href='https://english.nv.ua/nation/ukraine-says-moscow-region-hit-in-largest-drone-attack-of-war-50608630.html'>NV</a>)</li><li>Russian Foreign Ministry: Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova called the drone barrage a “mass terrorist attack” and linked it to EU financing of Kyiv, according to TASS. (<a href='https://www.newarab.com/news/ukraine-drones-kill-four-moscow-faces-biggest-attack-year'>The New Arab</a>)</li><li>Ukraine’s Unmanned Forces: Commander Robert Brovdi told AFP before the strikes that Ukraine’s priority was to expand long-range strikes against a wide range of military targets. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2001019/mass-ukrainian-drone-barrage-kills-four-in-russia'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1tgaczf/ukraine_conducts_largescale_drone_strikes_on/'>Ukraine conducts large-scale drone strikes on Russia, killing 4 and wounding a dozen others</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/world/europe/russia-ukraine-strikes-moscow.html'>Wave of Ukrainian Strikes Kills at Least 4, Russia Says</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/ukraine-drones-kill-four-in-russia-moscow-faces-biggest-attack-in-over-a-year4'>Ukraine drones kill four in Russia; Moscow faces biggest attack in over a year</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/a